 "plan": {
  "angle": "The results for this query are downloadable Word, PDF and Excel PIP templates and HR guides that list the sections (the gap, the expected standard, goals, support, timeline, signatures). A file stops at the meeting. This page shows a working PIP form that keeps going after it: goals that will not save without a number and a date, the coaching the company promised logged as it happens, a reminder before each check-in that carries only a link, and an HR view of every open plan and its end date, all saved to a database the employer owns. No legal or HR-law advice; the copy gives instructions, not requirements.",
  "tab_stories": [
   "At Garnock Office Supply, sales manager Dana Kilburn writes a 60-day plan for rep #207, and the form refuses a goal until it has a number and a due date: 8 booked demos a month and 50 logged calls a week.",
   "At Hattersley Software, team lead Joel Ravenscroft logs the 2 coaching sessions a week the plan promised agent #3318, whose QA score has moved from 71% toward the 85% target.",
   "At Cobbridge Logistics, supervisor Nadia Truscott gets an email 2 days before each biweekly check-in for picker #1046, with a link and no details, and marks the error goal met at 3 errors against a limit of 4.",
   "At Vintry Pharmacy, HR lead Gail Wainscott sees 7 open plans across 4 stores; 2 end this week, and one passed its end date with no outcome recorded, so it sits at the top in red."
  ],
